Depends: podman, dosfstools, e2fsprogs, btrfs-progs, cryptsetup-bin, util-linux, xfsprogs, skopeo, polkit
Description: bootc disk installer backend
 Command-line backend for bootc-based OS installers. Reads a JSON recipe
 describing the target disk, encryption, bootloader and image source, then
 performs all installation steps: partition, format, LUKS setup, mount,
 bootc install to-filesystem, post-configuration, and finalize.
 .
 fisherman is invoked by graphical frontends such as bootc-installer via
 pkexec. It supports GRUB2 and systemd-boot stacks, LUKS+TPM2 encryption,
 btrfs/xfs/ext4 filesystems, and offline installs from a local OCI store.
